{"schema":1,"fm":{"schema":1,"id":"set-up-lab-cleaning-rota","kind":"prompt","title":"Set up a lab duties rota","description":"Sets up a fair rota for shared lab duties such as cleaning, autoclaving, waste runs, stock checks and equipment upkeep, with task cards, frequencies, cover rules and sign-off.","category":"lab-work","version":"1.0.0","status":"incubating","stage":["operate"],"role":["researcher","operations-manager","student"],"requires":["none"],"inputs":["text","notes"],"output":["plan","table","checklist"],"risk":"read-only","invocation":"user","effort":"quick","interaction":"one-shot","model_tier":"mid","reasoning":"optional","level":"beginner","depth":"specific","tags":["lab-duties","rota","lab-cleaning","shared-equipment","lab-culture"],"pairs_with":{"prompts":["set-up-equipment-booking-rules","set-up-reagent-inventory","write-lab-induction-checklist"],"personas":["lab-manager"]},"args":[{"name":"duties","description":"The shared jobs in the lab and roughly how long each takes, for example \"empty autoclave, restock tips, clean water bath, check incubator CO2, take waste out\".","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"people","description":"Who is in the rota (count, roles, part-time or visiting status) and any constraints, for example \"students teach on Tuesdays\".","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"problems","description":"What goes wrong now, for example \"same two people do everything\" or \"water bath never cleaned\". Optional.","type":"text"}],"output_contract":{"format":"markdown","sections":["Duty list","Rota","Task cards","Cover and swaps","Checking it works"]},"authorship":"ai-assisted","authors":["gabrielanhaia"],"last_reviewed":"2026-10-11","changelog":[{"version":"1.0.0","note":"First version."}]},"body":"<context>\nShared lab duties fall to the most conscientious few unless the rota is explicit, fair by time not by task count, visible, and checked. Each duty needs a short task card that says what \"done\" looks like, because \"clean the water bath\" means different things to different people. Safety-relevant duties (eyewash checks, fume hood sash checks, waste collection) need a record, and duties needing training only go to trained people.\n</context>\n\n<task>\n<duties>\n{{duties}}\n</duties>\n\n<people>\n{{people}}\n</people>\n{{#problems}}\n\n<problems>\n{{problems}}\n</problems>\n{{/problems}}\n\n1. Duty list: each duty with frequency, time it takes, training needed and whether it needs a written record.\n2. Rota: a schedule that balances total minutes per person over a cycle, respects the constraints, and pairs new members with experienced ones on unfamiliar duties.\n3. Task cards: for each duty, steps and what \"done\" looks like in a few lines.\n4. Cover and swaps: how to swap, what happens at holidays, and who covers when someone forgets.\n5. Checking it works: a sign-off sheet, a monthly glance by the lab manager, and a review after one cycle.\n</task>\n\n<constraints>\n- Balance by time, and show the minutes per person.\n- Do not assign duties needing training to untrained people.\n- Keep the tone collegial; this is not a disciplinary system.\n</constraints>\n\n<output_format>\n## Duty list\n| Duty | Frequency | Minutes | Training | Record |\n## Rota\n## Task cards\n## Cover and swaps\n## Checking it works\n</output_format>","steps":[]}
